<div style="margin-left: 36pt; font-weight: normal; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-size: 10pt; font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; text-transform: none;">The intrinsic value of options exercised during the years ended
        December 31, 2022 and 2021 was $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsExercisesInPeriodTotalIntrinsicValue" id="Fact_9f4de66ed46348ba9a6b55e96cbf1ff3" contextRef="c20220101to20221231" unitRef="U001" decimals="0" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">3,306</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardOptionsExercisesInPeriodTotalIntrinsicValue" id="Fact_b874239552fe4fc38bf599f24e1e1b47" contextRef="c20210101to20211231" unitRef="U001" decimals="0" scale="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">159,062</ix:nonFraction>,
        respectively. The intrinsic values represent the dollar value of the exercised stock options whereby the fair market value of the underlying common stock exceeded the exercise price of the stock option as of the exercise date.</div>
</ix:continuation>
